{"id": 22, "ts": 1780445893.3191183, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate the enthusiasm for Candidate\u202fC\u2019s rapid decision\u2011making and strong attention to detail, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the safer overall choice for a long\u2011distance pilot.\u202fB\u2019s very conscientious nature and proven ability to handle stress well directly address the operational reliability and stress\u2011resilience criteria that are non\u2011negotiable for international flights.\u202fHis solid skill in assessing weather conditions and excellent computer proficiency are also critical for the complex, technology\u2011driven environments we operate in.\nWhile I acknowledge the concerns raised about B\u2019s occasional pretentiousness and tone, these are communication style issues that can be mitigated through cockpit crew\u2011resource\u2011management training. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC, despite quick decision\u2011making, shows difficulty communicating ideas, is regarded as egocentric, and is not very willing to pursue further education\u2014traits that raise red flags for crew cooperation, professional communication, and adaptability. Given the balance of strengths and mitigable weaknesses, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB."}
